librevenge: an OLE header whose block shift is out of range must be refused, not asserted on (FF-6 option C).

RVNGOLEStream.cpp: Header::load() clamps the 16-bit shifts from the file to 31, and compute_block_size() then did assert(shift < 31): a header with a
shift of 31 or more (any hostile OLE2 file) aborted the process in a build without NDEBUG, and shifted by 31 in one with it. valid() already rejects
such a header (shift_bbat >= 31), but only after compute_block_size(). Now compute_block_size() leaves both sizes at 0 for an out-of-range shift and
valid() refuses first, before any division by them. Found by seeded mutation of real legacy files on the standalone legacy module (3 of 3 aborts).
Upstream candidate for the owner: upstream-issues/librevenge-ole-header-shift-assert.md.

--- a/src/lib/RVNGOLEStream.cpp	2026-11-08 23:58:16.582540706 +0000
+++ b/src/lib/RVNGOLEStream.cpp	2026-11-08 23:58:16.584699074 +0000
@@ -128,8 +128,14 @@
 	Header();
 	void compute_block_size()
 	{
-		assert(m_shift_bbat < 31);
-		assert(m_shift_sbat < 31);
+		// A header from a file can carry any shift (load() clamps it to 31): a shift of 31 or more is not a valid OLE
+		// header and valid() rejects it, so do not abort on it (assert) and do not shift by it.
+		if (m_shift_bbat >= 31 || m_shift_sbat >= 31)
+		{
+			m_size_bbat = 0;
+			m_size_sbat = 0;
+			return;
+		}
 		m_size_bbat = 1 << m_shift_bbat;
 		m_size_sbat = 1 << m_shift_sbat;
 	}
@@ -753,6 +759,8 @@
 
 bool librevenge::Header::valid(const unsigned long fileSize) const
 {
+	// compute_block_size() leaves the sizes at 0 for a shift out of range: refuse before any division by them
+	if (m_shift_bbat >= 31 || m_shift_sbat >= 31 || m_size_bbat == 0 || m_size_sbat == 0) return false;
 	if (m_threshold != 4096) return false;
 	// there must be at least the header, one bat sector and one dirent sector in the file
 	if ((fileSize / m_size_bbat) < 3) return false;
